print(prices)
```
wrong[[10, 25, 40]]: The loop assigns to `prices[i]`, which changes the list itself: each item drops by 5.
wrong[5\n20\n35]: The print is after the loop, so it runs once and shows the whole list.
wrong[[5, 20]]: `range(len(prices))` is `range(3)`: indexes 0, 1 and 2, so all three items change.
